MISTRAL.text:
```json
[
  {
    "severity": "high",
    "area": "state management",
    "issue": "No validation for duplicate model names/vendors when adding/editing models. This can lead to confusion and incorrect comparisons.",
    "fix": "Add a check in `saveModel()` to verify that the name+vendor combination doesn't already exist (unless editing the same model). Show a toast error if duplicate is detected."
  },
  {
    "severity": "medium",
    "area": "edge case",
    "issue": "Empty `ctxTokens` input in edit modal (e.g., user clears the field) results in `NaN` context score calculation, which propagates to final score.",
    "fix": "In `contextScore()`, add a guard: `if (isNaN(tokens) || tokens <= 0) return 0;`"
  },
  {
    "severity": "medium",
    "area": "edge case",
    "issue": "Negative or non-numeric values in numeric edit fields (e.g., `f_reasoning`) are not properly sanitized, leading to `NaN` scores.",
    "fix": "In `saveModel()`, ensure all numeric fields are clamped to 0-100: `const num = id => clamp(parseInt(document.getElementById(id).value) || 0, 0, 100);`"
  },
  {
    "severity": "medium",
    "area": "state management",
    "issue": "`prevOrder` is not reset when models are added/deleted, causing incorrect rank-change deltas on subsequent renders.",
    "fix": "Reset `prevOrder = []` in `saveModel()` and `deleteModel()` after modifying `MODELS`."
  },
  {
    "severity": "low",
    "area": "escaping",
    "issue": "Vendor name in edit modal is not escaped when rendered back into the input field, creating XSS risk if vendor name contains HTML.",
    "fix": "Wrap `m.vendor` in `escapeHtml()` in the edit modal template: `value=\"${escapeHtml(m.vendor)}\"`"
  },
  {
    "severity": "low",
    "area": "edge case",
    "issue": "Context token input in edit modal allows non-numeric characters (e.g., commas), which are stripped but may confuse users.",
    "fix": "Add `inputmode=\"numeric\"` and `pattern=\"[0-9]*\"` to the context token input field to enforce numeric keypad on mobile and basic validation."
  }
]
```

